'''Rogues' chests''' are located in the [[Rogues' Castle]] at approximately level 54 [[Wilderness]]. They require 84 [[Thieving]] to open. Players must use the "Search for traps" option from the right-click menu to open it successfully. There are three chests total which each take 34 [[ticks|game ticks]] (20.4 seconds) to reset. Possible loot includes 16 unique stackable items, an unnoted [[Prayer potion|2-dose prayer potion]] (commonly consumed to extend trips), and [[Clue scroll (hard)|hard clue scrolls]]. 

Upon successfully unlocking a chest, the player is granted 701.7 Thieving [[experience]]. If the player has completed the [[Wilderness Diary#Medium|medium Wilderness diary]], it will provide loot including [[runes]], noted uncut [[gems]], [[Mining|ores]], [[blighted#Item|blighted food]], and [[dragonstone]]s. Completing the [[Wilderness Diary#hard|hard Wilderness diary]] will provide around 20% extra GE value in loot and is therefore highly recommended. 

Along with [[hellhound]]s, the chest is one of the best sources for [[Clue scroll (hard)|hard clue scrolls]] in the game when an [[Ring of wealth (i)|imbued ring of wealth]] is worn. However, on any death, the ring of wealth will lose its imbued status. 

Successfully stealing from a chest is an elite task in the [[Wilderness Diary]].

