==Transportation==
'''{{Colour|red|Warning:}} The chests are located within the deep Wilderness. In addition to the threat of player-killers, the [[Chaos Elemental]], which has a very accurate attack which ignores protection prayers and hits up to 28, may wander to the entrance of the Rogues' Castle.''' '''Always check your risk prior to entering the Wilderness and do not bring items you are unwilling to lose.'''

There are several options to get to the Rogues' Chests:
* Teleporting to Level-50 Wilderness using a [[Wilderness Obelisk]] is the fastest method to get there. It is recommended to have completed the [[hard Wilderness Diary]] in order to set their destination when using the obelisk.
*Players can use the [[Ancient Magicks|Ancient spellbook's]] [[Annakarl Teleport]] or an [[Annakarl teleport (tablet)|Annakarl teleport tablet]] to the [[Demonic Ruins]]. The player can then run east to the gate and then north-west to the castle.
*Teleporting to the [[Fountain of Rune]] using the [[Wilderness sword 3]] (one daily teleport) or [[Wilderness sword 4|4]] (unlimited) puts the player a similar distance away as the Annakarl Teleport.
*The [[Lever (Edgeville)|Edgeville lever]] teleports the player west of the [[Resource Area]] deep in the [[Wilderness]]. The player can run east to get to the castle, but this route requires passing through a [[Web]] and has a higher chance of encountering the Chaos Elemental. 

==Strategy==
{{Main|Chest (Rogues' Castle)/Strategies}}
The courtyard with the chests contains numerous non-aggressive level-135 [[rogue]]s. Once a chest is opened, the rogues will all attack the player. The rogues are moderately accurate and have a max hit of 15, but their damage can be completely blocked by [[Protect from Melee]]. For sustainable sessions, it is highly recommended to have a [[Prayer]] level of at least 43 to use Protect from Melee.

Player-killers are extremely common at the rogue's castle, and frequently [[world hop]] looking for victims, often in the courtyard itself or the shed just east of the chests. To try to keep the valuable loot, it's recommended for players to use a non-deadly [[:Category:Self-damaging items|self-damaging item]] such as a [[dwarven rock cake]] or [[locator orb]] to continuously keep their hitpoints as low as possible. Immediately on spotting a player-killer, the player should then use an [[Araxyte venom sac]], which deals 4 damage and will kill the player if they've kept their hitpoints below that. Otherwise, the player can also disable Protect from Melee and let the rogues kill them instead, but this is much less reliable.

While the player is unlocking the chest, which takes at least a few ticks, no other action can be initiated including self-damage. Switching protection prayers will occur once the chest is looted, but items will need to be clicked again. For this reason, it isn't always possible to force a [[Pvm death|PvM death]] even with a quick reaction on seeing a player-killer. 

Note that if a player-killer manages to cast a spell, shoot an arrow, or attacks with melee, a self-inflicted or monster death will almost certainly count as a [[Pvp death|PvP death]] even if the spell, projectile, or weapon deals a zero hitsplat. Only the three items protected on death will kept. 

==Rewards==
[[File:Stealing from rogues' chests.png|thumb|300px|Rogues attacking the player upon a successful loot.]]
Opening the chests continuously without interruption yields at least 300,000 Thieving experience per hour. A handful of interruptions in an hour, whether from banking or player-killers, reduces the hourly experience to around 260,000 to 280,000. If the player can tolerate the risk, this activity offers the fastest Thieving experience in the game. 

Without interruption and with the Hard Diary completed, it takes between 10 and 15 minutes to reach around 500,000 gold in loot plus the occasional [[Scroll box (hard)|hard scroll box]]. The possible reward of [[dragonstone]]s makes the chest a popular method for [[Ironman Mode|Ironmen]] and players looking to make [[dragonstone jewellery]]. The [[Law rune|Law runes]] given are prodigious and can be very helpful for adding locations to the [[Portal nexus]]. [[Nature rune|Nature]] and law runes will account for around 35% of the [[Grand Exchange]] value of the loot, followed by [[Uncut diamond|Uncut diamonds]], coins, and [[Coal]]. 

